
<Defs xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="rimworld DefsSchema.xsd" xmlns="rimworld">

	<!--
		Hidden toughness hediff for Big & Small-added body parts.

		B&S-added parts (wings from thingDefSwap, tails, extra arms) use the pawn's
		own HealthScale, which vanilla scales off the RACE's baseHealthScale. A
		dragon's wings are as tough as she is (x1.0) - no bug. A tiny race's
		added parts would inherit her fragile HP, so a race tracker applies this
		hediff to the added part (applyPartHediff) with a partEfficiency bump.

		Hidden from the Health tab: pure plumbing, not a condition the player
		should read. The first user is PMM insect races (chitin limbs); the flight
		gene applies it to BS_Wing as well, so dragon wings share the same
		toughness plumbing as every other momo body part.
	-->
	<HediffDef>
		<defName>PMM_Hediff_PartToughness</defName>
		<label>reinforced body part</label>
		<description>Chitin-reinforced flesh: this part is tougher than the rest of her body.</description>
		<hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass>
		<scenarioCanAdd>false</scenarioCanAdd>
		<isBad>false</isBad>
		<everCurableByItem>false</everCurableByItem>
		<addedPartProps>
			<!-- Not a prosthetic - it must not out-tough the body it grows on
			     in the replace-part maths, only add a flat efficiency bump. -->
			<betterThanNatural>false</betterThanNatural>
			<partEfficiency>1.25</partEfficiency>
		</addedPartProps>
	</HediffDef>

</Defs>
